std::size_t previous = bytes_acquired_.fetch_add(raw_size, std::memory_order_acq_rel);

if (previous + raw_size > /* extract raw value from budget ceiling */)
{
    bytes_acquired_.fetch_sub(raw_size, std::memory_order_relaxed);
    throw std::bad_alloc();
}
```

Same budget-gate pattern the allocator uses for chunk count, just applied to byte totals. The `Bytes` type appears at every human-facing boundary and disappears at every hardware-facing boundary.

