**Virtual dispatch (what you're intuiting)**

A base `MemoryScope` with a virtual `refill_and_pop()`. A `RootScope` derives from it and overrides `refill_and_pop()` to call the function pointer into `MemoryCore`. Non-root scopes use the base implementation which cascades to `parent_scope_`.

